	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "tYYh1aZHjzd9kaUE2",
			"name": "Custodian Attribute Modifiers",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Custodian stands 2.5-3 m tall, built from infancy on hormonal and surgical regimes far more individually tailored than a Chapter's gene-seed batch process. Chris Wraight's Custodes novels (The Emperor's Legion, Watchers of the Throne) and current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background are consistent that a Custodian outclasses a Space Marine the way a Space Marine outclasses an unaugmented human - faster, stronger, more perceptive, and immeasurably more skilled from centuries of training against the best the Imperium has ever fielded.\n\nDesign: Framework targets: ST 40 (with the SM +1 cost break), DX 20 with training, IQ 13, HT 16, Will 16, HP ~50, Basic Speed well above an Astartes. Increased Strength +30 (B14, 10/level, 300) for ST 40; per B18's Size and Strength Table a creature whose SM matches its actual bulk gets a cost break on ST, and SM +1 gives -10%, so 300 x 0.9 = 270. Increased Dexterity +9 (B14, 20/level, 180) for DX 19, raised at the user's direction so a trained Custodian reaches DX 20, well above an Astartes' DX 16. Basic Move +4 (B17, 5/level, 20): Custodes cross a battlefield far faster than any human, matching the Astartes speed boost with their own greater Basic Speed on top. Increased Intelligence +3 (B16, 20/level, 60) for IQ 13. Increased Health +6 (B15, 10/level, 60) for HT 16, two points above the Astartes HT 14. Increased Will +3 (B16, 5/level, 15) on top of IQ for Will 16, matching the framework's explicit split between IQ 13 and Will 16 - a Custodian's raw wit is merely excellent, but nothing moves his resolve. Extra Hit Points +10 (B16, 2/level, 20) for HP ~50 (40 base from ST, +10). Increased Basic Speed +1.50 (B17, 5 points per 0.25 level, 30) stacks with the formula-derived Basic Speed of (19+16)/4 = 8.75 for a final 10.25 - well above an Astartes' 8.75, matching \"faster reflexes ... Basic Speed well above an Astartes.\" SM +1 is the framework's own figure for an unarmoured Custodian and carries no further point cost beyond the ST break already taken above. 270+180+60+60+15+20+30+20 = 655 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"base_points": 655,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "st",
					"amount": 30
				},
				{
