		{
			"id": "to2_uVEpVZ7FmuoEB",
			"name": "Unfazeable",
			"reference": "B99",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Custodian has stood in the Sanctum Imperialis for ten thousand years, fought Horus's own Sons of Horus, boarded daemon-infested hulks, and duelled things with no right to exist. Black Library and Codex background never show a Custodian rattled, hesitant, or surprised by anything short of the direct will of the Emperor.\n\nDesign: Unfazeable (B99, 15 points): full immunity to Fear and to being surprised, stronger than the Fearlessness the Astartes package uses, matching the framework's flat \"immune to fear\" instruction rather than a leveled resistance.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "t7p6qSSgBLrhBxHES",
			"name": "Unaging",
			"reference": "B17",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Ten Thousand have served since before the Imperium existed; named Custodians such as Valerian, Aleya, and the long-lived characters of Wraight's novels are treated as ancient by any human standard without any hint of physical decline. The exact biological mechanism (whether it is a one-off transformation or an ongoing process) is not detailed in the fiction consulted for this build.\n\nDesign: Unaging (B17, 15 points): no HT penalties or death checks from old age, matching \"lives for millennia\" without claiming a specific immortality mechanism the sources don't describe.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "tMovzAwPTb5rguK3T",
			"name": "Combat Reflexes",
			"reference": "B43",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Centuries of drilling against the finest opponents the Imperium can offer (including each other) leave a Custodian essentially unshakeable in combat, never fumbling a reaction to a sudden threat.\n\nDesign: Combat Reflexes (B43, 15 points), as the Astartes package.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "tN7wpQq6Kz0Hi-NAD",
			"name": "Custodian Senses",
			"reference": "B16",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Codex background credits Custodians with reflexes and situational awareness that let them track and parry attacks other elites simply cannot perceive in time; this is modelled as raw Perception rather than the itemised acute-sense organs the Astartes package uses, since no source breaks a Custodian's senses down organ by organ.\n\nDesign: Increased Perception +4 (B16, 5/level, 20 points): a broad \"notices everything\" bonus, deliberately not split into Astartes- style Acute Vision/Hearing/Smell packages since the fiction doesn't describe Custodian senses that granularly.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "TTa47VV3ndqTmYrhW",
			"name": "Custodian Regeneration",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Custodians shrug off and recover from wounds that would permanently cripple or kill an Astartes, a detail repeated across Wraight's novels (Custodians returning to duty from injuries a Space Marine would need months of Apothecarion care to survive). This project reads that as healing markedly faster than the Astartes package's Larraman's-Organ-based Rapid Healing, not as literal invulnerability.\n\nDesign: Regeneration (Slow, B80, 10 points) for passive healing even without rest, plus Very Rapid Healing (B80, 15 points, quadruple effective HT for natural recovery) for a step above the Astartes' plain Rapid Healing (double effective HT). 25 points total.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tynjgXgHjmmKMokA2",
					"name": "Regeneration (Slow)",
					"reference": "B80",
					"local_notes": "Recovers 1 HP per 12 hours even without rest or first aid.",
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "t-NKq3Oxd_y_I3Mnd",
					"name": "Very Rapid Healing",
					"reference": "B80",
					"base_points": 15
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TTzE6nu3rFBu2D5Ex",
			"name": "Custodian Constitution",
			"local_notes": "Lore: No single source itemises separate anti-toxin organs for Custodians the way Codex Astartes background does for the Preomnor and Oolitic Kidney; what the fiction consistently shows is a Custodian simply shrugging off poisons, plagues, and pain that would down anyone else outright.\n\nDesign: Resistant (B81), Very Common: Metabolic Hazards (disease, poison, toxins, radiation sickness and the like), Immunity tier - base 30, x1 for Immunity = 30 points, deliberately a single unified trait rather than the Astartes package's several organ-specific ones (Preomnor 10 + Oolitic Kidney 15 + part of Melanchromic Organ 11 = 36 split across three separate hazards): a Custodian's constitution doesn't have gaps between what different organs happen to cover. High Pain Threshold (B59, 10 points) as the Astartes package. 40 points total.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tyZmgg8EYdzxvB9b0",
					"name": "Resistant to Disease and Toxins",
					"reference": "B81",
					"local_notes": "Resistant (Very Common: Disease, Poison, Toxins, etc.), Immunity.",
					"base_points": 30
				},
				{
					"id": "tY6jSBPylwMPPKbir",
					"name": "High Pain Threshold",
					"reference": "B59",
					"base_points": 10
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TjPZQ_0h0VHp8fSpL",
			"name": "Custodian Physiology",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Legio Custodes: the Emperor's personal bodyguard, each Custodian individually created rather than mass-produced from a Chapter's gene-seed, and never numbering more than a few thousand in ten thousand years. Chris Wraight's Custodes novels and current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background are the primary sources for this file; Horus Heresy-era material (e.g. Master of Mankind) is used for the Custodes' role and demeanour during the Great Crusade and Heresy, not for anything this file treats as a hard number.\n\nDesign: 655 (Attribute Modifiers) + 15 (Unfazeable) + 15 (Unaging) + 15 (Combat Reflexes) + 20 (Custodian Senses) + 25 (Regeneration) + 40 (Constitution) + 20 (Enhanced Move 1) = 805 points of physiology alone, before oath, rank, or skills - see the Custodian Guardian and Shield-Captain templates. This comfortably clears \"outclasses a Space Marine the way a Space Marine outclasses a Guardsman\" in raw point terms (an Astartes package is 563) as well as in the attribute targets themselves.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"container_type": "ancestry",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "t6VeG4s-mvfIkthPf",
					"name": "Custodian Attribute Modifiers",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A Custodian stands 2.5-3 m tall, built from infancy on hormonal and surgical regimes far more individually tailored than a Chapter's gene-seed batch process. Chris Wraight's Custodes novels (The Emperor's Legion, Watchers of the Throne) and current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background are consistent that a Custodian outclasses a Space Marine the way a Space Marine outclasses an unaugmented human - faster, stronger, more perceptive, and immeasurably more skilled from centuries of training against the best the Imperium has ever fielded.\n\nDesign: Framework targets: ST 40 (with the SM +1 cost break), DX 20 with training, IQ 13, HT 16, Will 16, HP ~50, Basic Speed well above an Astartes. Increased Strength +30 (B14, 10/level, 300) for ST 40; per B18's Size and Strength Table a creature whose SM matches its actual bulk gets a cost break on ST, and SM +1 gives -10%, so 300 x 0.9 = 270. Increased Dexterity +9 (B14, 20/level, 180) for DX 19, raised at the user's direction so a trained Custodian reaches DX 20, well above an Astartes' DX 16. Basic Move +4 (B17, 5/level, 20): Custodes cross a battlefield far faster than any human, matching the Astartes speed boost with their own greater Basic Speed on top. Increased Intelligence +3 (B16, 20/level, 60) for IQ 13. Increased Health +6 (B15, 10/level, 60) for HT 16, two points above the Astartes HT 14. Increased Will +3 (B16, 5/level, 15) on top of IQ for Will 16, matching the framework's explicit split between IQ 13 and Will 16 - a Custodian's raw wit is merely excellent, but nothing moves his resolve. Extra Hit Points +10 (B16, 2/level, 20) for HP ~50 (40 base from ST, +10). Increased Basic Speed +1.50 (B17, 5 points per 0.25 level, 30) stacks with the formula-derived Basic Speed of (19+16)/4 = 8.75 for a final 10.25 - well above an Astartes' 8.75, matching \"faster reflexes ... Basic Speed well above an Astartes.\" SM +1 is the framework's own figure for an unarmoured Custodian and carries no further point cost beyond the ST break already taken above. 270+180+60+60+15+20+30+20 = 655 points.",
